<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions bonds worth 79 mln rupees.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions bonds worth 79 mln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it auctioned three-year, five-year and 10-year maturity federal invesment bonds (FIBs) worth 79 million rupees on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bank said it accepted all bids worth 20 million rupees at par for the three-year maturity bonds, 4.0 million for the five-year and 55 million for 10-year bonds.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
